# {{name}} (Local embedded Claude wrapper)

> Thin Claude Code discovery wrapper. The real skill lives in this repository and must not be copied or edited here.

When this skill runs:

1. From the consuming project root, resolve this repository's embedded source path (normally `./codex` for this checkout), or use `UNREAL_MCP_5_6_1_ROOT`.
2. Read the original skill body at `{{original_skill_path}}`.
3. Read `{{references_path}}` and load the linked workflow, policy, project, or role docs as instructed.
4. Follow the original instructions with these reader substitutions:
   - The Codex `$skill-name` invocation syntax -> invoke the matching Claude Code skill, or read that skill's `SKILL.md` and follow it.
   - "Codex" in source text -> the current Claude Code agent.
5. Do not modify the original skill package while acting through the wrapper unless the user explicitly asks to maintain the skill itself.

Re-run the local Claude sync tool only when original skill frontmatter changes or the project allowlist changes. Body and reference edits are read live from this repository.
